# System Architecture & Microservices Patterns

## **CRITICAL: Microservices Design Principles**

### **Service Boundaries**

Each service owns its domain and database:

```
auth-service/     → Authentication & Authorization
user-service/     → User Profile Management
shipment-service/ → Shipment Tracking & Management
support-service/  → Help Desk & Support Tickets
platform-service/ → E-commerce Platform Integrations
api-gateway/      → Request Routing & Rate Limiting
```

### **Database Per Service**

**MANDATORY**: Each service has its own database:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Service-specific database
// auth-service/prisma/schema.prisma
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL") // logistics_auth database
}

// ✅ CORRECT: Service-specific database
// user-service/prisma/schema.prisma
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL") // logistics_users database
}
```

## **API Communication Patterns**

### **RESTful API Design**

All services MUST follow RESTful conventions:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: RESTful routes
router.get("/users", getAllUsers); // GET collection
router.get("/users/:id", getUserById); // GET single resource
router.post("/users", createUser); // CREATE resource
router.put("/users/:id", updateUser); // UPDATE resource (full)
router.patch("/users/:id", patchUser); // UPDATE resource (partial)
router.delete("/users/:id", deleteUser); // DELETE resource

// ✅ CORRECT: Nested resources
router.get("/users/:id/shipments", getUserShipments);
router.post("/users/:id/shipments", createShipmentForUser);
```

### **API Gateway Pattern**

All external requests MUST go through API Gateway:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: API Gateway routing
// api-gateway/server.js
app.use(
  "/api/v1/auth",
  createProxyMiddleware({
    target: "http://auth-service:8001",
    pathRewrite: { "^/api/v1/auth": "" },
  })
);

app.use(
  "/api/v1/users",
  authenticateToken, // Middleware applied at gateway
  createProxyMiddleware({
    target: "http://user-service:8002",
    pathRewrite: { "^/api/v1/users": "" },
  })
);
```

### **Inter-Service Communication**

Services communicate via HTTP APIs (never direct database access):

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Service-to-service HTTP calls
// user-service calling auth-service
async function validateToken(token) {
  const response = await fetch(`${AUTH_SERVICE_URL}/validate`, {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
  });
  return response.json();
}

// ❌ WRONG: Direct database access across services
const authUser = await authPrisma.user.findFirst({ where: { id } }); // FORBIDDEN
```

## **MANDATORY: Error Handling Patterns**

### **Consistent Error Response Format**

All services MUST use the same error format:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Standard error response
const errorResponse = {
  success: false,
  error: {
    code: "USER_NOT_FOUND",
    message: "User with ID 123 not found",
    details: {},
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    service: "user-service",
  },
};

// ✅ CORRECT: Success response format
const successResponse = {
  success: true,
  data: {
    /* response data */
  },
  meta: {
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    service: "user-service",
  },
};
```

### **Centralized Error Handling Middleware**

Each service MUST have error handling middleware:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Centralized error handler
// middleware/errorHandler.js
function errorHandler(error, req, res, next) {
  const { statusCode = 500, message, code = "INTERNAL_ERROR" } = error;

  res.status(statusCode).json({
    success: false,
    error: {
      code,
      message,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      service: process.env.SERVICE_NAME,
      requestId: req.id,
    },
  });
}
```

## **Authentication & Authorization Patterns**

### **JWT Token Pattern**

Centralized authentication with distributed authorization:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: JWT middleware in each service
// middleware/auth.js
async function authenticateToken(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(" ")[1];

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(401).json({
      success: false,
      error: { code: "NO_TOKEN", message: "Access token required" },
    });
  }

  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET);
    req.user = payload;
    next();
  } catch (error) {
    return res.status(403).json({
      success: false,
      error: { code: "INVALID_TOKEN", message: "Token is invalid" },
    });
  }
}
```

### **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**

Implement consistent RBAC across all services:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Role-based middleware
function requireRole(roles) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!req.user || !roles.includes(req.user.role)) {
      return res.status(403).json({
        success: false,
        error: {
          code: "INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS",
          message: `Required role: ${roles.join(" or ")}`,
        },
      });
    }
    next();
  };
}

// Usage:
router.get(
  "/admin/users",
  authenticateToken,
  requireRole(["Admin", "Operations"]),
  getAllUsers
);
```

## **Data Validation Patterns**

### **Joi Schema Validation**

Every endpoint MUST validate input data:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Joi validation schemas
// validation/userSchemas.js
const createUserSchema = Joi.object({
  email: Joi.string().email().required(),
  password: Joi.string().min(8).required(),
  role: Joi.string().valid("Admin", "Client", "Operations").default("Client"),
  profile: Joi.object({
    firstName: Joi.string().required(),
    lastName: Joi.string().required(),
    phone: Joi.string().pattern(/^\+91[0-9]{10}$/),
  }).required(),
});

// ✅ CORRECT: Validation middleware
function validateBody(schema) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const { error, value } = schema.validate(req.body);
    if (error) {
      return res.status(400).json({
        success: false,
        error: {
          code: "VALIDATION_ERROR",
          message: error.details[0].message,
          details: error.details,
        },
      });
    }
    req.body = value; // Use validated/sanitized data
    next();
  };
}
```

## **Database Patterns**

### **Prisma Schema Organization**

Each service's Prisma schema should be self-contained:

```prisma
// ✅ CORRECT: Service-specific schema
// auth-service/prisma/schema.prisma
model User {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())
  email           String   @unique
  passwordHash    String
  role            Role     @default(CLIENT)
  isActive        Boolean  @default(true)
  lastLoginAt     DateTime?
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt

  // Service-specific relationships only
  sessions        Session[]
  auditLogs       AuditLog[]

  @@map("users")
}

enum Role {
  ADMIN
  FINANCE
  OPERATIONS
  CLIENT
  SUPPORT
}
```

### **Migration Management**

Each service manages its own migrations:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT: Service-specific migrations
cd backend/auth-service && npx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_roles
cd backend/user-service && npx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_profiles

# ✅ CORRECT: Production migrations in Docker
command: sh -c "npx prisma migrate deploy && pnpm run start"
```

## **Logging & Monitoring Patterns**

### **Structured Logging**

All services MUST use structured logging:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Winston structured logging
const logger = winston.createLogger({
  format: winston.format.combine(
    winston.format.timestamp(),
    winston.format.json()
  ),
  defaultMeta: {
    service: process.env.SERVICE_NAME,
    version: process.env.SERVICE_VERSION,
  },
});

// ✅ CORRECT: Log usage
logger.info("User created successfully", {
  userId: user.id,
  email: user.email,
  requestId: req.id,
  ipAddress: req.ip,
});
```

### **Health Check Endpoints**

Every service MUST have health checks:

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Health check implementation
router.get("/health", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    // Check database connection
    await prisma.$queryRaw`SELECT 1`;

    // Check Redis connection (if used)
    await redisClient.ping();

    res.json({
      status: "healthy",
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      service: process.env.SERVICE_NAME,
      version: process.env.SERVICE_VERSION,
      uptime: process.uptime(),
      dependencies: {
        database: "connected",
        redis: "connected",
      },
    });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(503).json({
      status: "unhealthy",
      error: error.message,
    });
  }
});
```
